  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** $P$ is a pentagon, **then** $P$ is a polygon.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ $P$ is a pentagon.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ $P$ is a polygon.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A\u21d2B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\u00acA\u21d2\u00acB.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $\u00acA:$ $P$ is not a pentagon.\n\n- $\u00acB:$ $P$ is not a polygon.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If $P$ is not a pentagon, then $P$ is not a polygon.",
